From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:49:48 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add retention job and its integration tests

src/auditflow/orchestration/retention.py was already in the working tree
(untracked, never committed, no tests); it is committed here unmodified.
It implements the policy in architecture.md "Phase 3+4":

  conversation_turns: viewer 7 days, employee/ceo/admin 30 days, by the
                      user's current role (unknown user -> viewer window)
  audit_log:          90 days for everyone, independent of the turns row

Day counts are overridable with RETENTION_VIEWER_DAYS / RETENTION_STAFF_DAYS /
RETENTION_AUDIT_DAYS (invalid values raise instead of silently defaulting).
Deletes run in batches, one short transaction each. Idempotent; --dry-run only
counts. Run: python -m src.auditflow.orchestration.retention [--dry-run],
schedulable from cron or RQ (purge_expired() takes no required arguments).

tests/integration/test_retention.py (27 tests, real Postgres) seeds rows at
exact ages and covers: viewer vs staff windows at the same age, window
boundaries, unknown users, role changes between runs, audit_log's independent
90-day rule, dry-run == real run, idempotency, batching edge cases (including
the exact-multiple case), env overrides and validation, and the CLI. Each
policy-bearing line of retention.py was mutated and a test failed every time.

